+Scope: read-only source inspection; no children, background work, provider calls, or repository changes.
+
+## Existing seam to preserve
+
+- `source/providers/openrouter-decisions.ts` is already the sole Decisions transport: it posts `{model,state,questions}` to `/api/alpha/decisions`, uses the configured OpenRouter key/base URL, and has a 10 s abort deadline.
+- `source/services/approval/decision-shadow.ts` is consumer-specific parsing for the existing approval comparison. Keep its approval policy and answer interpretation local; do not turn it into a generic shadow coordinator.
+- `source/services/approval/shell-auto-approval-evaluator.ts` establishes the required shadow semantics: opt-in, bounded in-flight work, fire-and-forget for interactive use, failures logged and swallowed, and no authority over the foreground decision.
+- Public hooks (`source/services/hooks/*`) are not the right extension mechanism. They intentionally expose privacy-filtered summaries, are awaited serially, permit callbacks to run after timeout, and carry no exact callable catalog or per-provider-request identity.
+
+## Narrow shared decision interface
+
+Refine the existing Decisions transport boundary, not the runtime orchestration:
+
+```ts
+type DecisionRequest = {
+  model: string;
+  state: unknown;
+  questions: Record<string, DecisionQuestion>;
+  signal?: AbortSignal;
+};
+
+type DecisionResponse = {
+  answers: Record<string, unknown>;
+  resolvedModel?: string;
+  usage?: unknown;
+  costUsd?: number | string;
+};
+
+interface DecisionClient {
+  decide(request: DecisionRequest): Promise<DecisionResponse>;
+}
+```
+
+The OpenRouter adapter should validate only the common envelope and retain optional provider metadata. Each shadow consumer owns its frozen/versioned prompt, question keys, and strict answer parser. Unknown/malformed answers are consumer failures, never defaults. Do not add a `Manager`, `Runner`, or behavior-changing result callback.
+
+Record transport evidence around this boundary: requested model, provider-resolved model when returned, monotonic duration, outcome (`completed|failed|cancelled|saturated`), and cost as an optional value. The current source has no proven Decisions usage/cost response contract, so absent cost must be logged as unknown/omitted, never `0` and never guessed from the foreground model catalog.
+
+## Tool-selection consumer: exact hook and evidence
+
+### Hook
+
+Use the application model-request boundary in `ApplicationRunLoop.#execute`, immediately after the `StreamedModelTurnRequest` is built and immediately before `model.stream(request)` (`source/services/agent-runtime/application-run-loop.ts`; today `requestPreparation.prepare(request)` occupies this exact point).
+
+This is the first point where all of these are simultaneously final for one dispatched request:
+
+- admitted steers and any boundary compaction are reflected in `request.input`;
+- provider/model and process-unique request ID are known;
+- critical wrap-up can correctly expose an empty catalog;
+- model-facing `request.tools` and executable `request.applicationTools` are fixed.
+
+Launch the shadow without awaiting it. Reconcile its prediction with the request's observed tool calls asynchronously by request ID. A text-only completion is an explicit `none` outcome. Do not put the model's selected outcome/tool calls into the prediction input.
+
+### Actual callable catalog
+
+`request.applicationTools` alone is insufficient: when `run_code` is present, `buildAgentTools()` returns only directly callable tools, while the wrapped built-ins are held by `run_code`'s bound registry and MCP definitions are created lazily.
