+
+- built-ins: the final wrapped registry after `bindRunCodeRegistry()` and after `RUN_CODE_PROHIBITED_TOOLS` filtering;
+- MCP: `createMcpCatalog()` over the turn-stable `McpToolSource.snapshot()`, ready servers only, after normalized-name collision removal;
+- direct-only tools: the final model-facing definitions returned by `buildAgentTools()`;
+- critical wrap-up: no candidates, matching the actual request.
+
+Do not parse `run_code.description`, use raw `getAgentDefinition()` tools, or concatenate MCP snapshots independently; each can disagree with execution. Preserve callable identity and route separately, e.g. `{name, callPath: 'direct'|'run_code', source: 'builtin'|'mcp', server?, originalName?, parameters, effect?, canRequireApproval?}`. MCP server state/collision diagnostics may be logged but must not be selectable candidates.
+
