+
+Turn stability already exists: `TurnStableMcpToolSource.beginTurn()` advances pending catalogs only at the next turn. Preserve that identity so prediction input and execution cannot drift mid-turn.
+
+## Provider-failure triage consumer: exact hook and evidence
+
+Hook the non-retry terminal branch of the per-request catch in `ApplicationRunLoop.#execute`, beside the existing failed/cancelled `ModelRequestCost` settlement and before rethrow. This sees the original error after in-loop retry policy has declined/exhausted retries and has the request ID, provider, model, service tier, attempt count, previous-response/chaining state, and cancellation signal.
+
+Build deterministic, sanitized evidence from existing contracts:
+
+- `classifyProviderFailure(error)` (`source/services/retry/provider-failure-classification.ts`): `errorKind`, safe `code`, integer `status`, `retryAfterMs`, bounded message, `retryable`;
+- `isClassifiedCancellation(error)`: strict cancellation/lifecycle distinction. Pure aborts are cancellation observations, not failures. Mixed abort+provider/network aggregates remain failures and must not be hidden;
+- in-loop retry decision/reason and attempts already spent;
+- request transport facts only (provider, requested model, tier, chaining present/disabled); no raw headers, credentials, request body, or user conversation.
+
+The triage result is observational classification only. It must not modify retry policy, throw in place of the provider error, suppress the original failure, or delay rethrow. Do not hook `turn.error`: it currently reports `unknown`, omits cancellations, lacks request identity, and sits after retry/recovery decisions.
+
+Lifecycle handling should mirror the existing approval shadow: a small shared in-flight cap, an explicit saturation log, deadline via the existing Decisions transport, and caught terminal rejection. Do not cancel a settled foreground turn merely to stop its shadow; cap plus deadline is sufficient and avoids adding ownership machinery. Process/session disposal may abort outstanding transport only if an existing owner can supply a signal without widening lifecycle interfaces.
+
+## Replay and measurement contracts
+
+Keep replay cases as versioned, non-private fixtures: `{caseId, consumer, promptVersion, evidence, expectedLabel}`. Expected labels must not be embedded in `state` or question text. Replay calls the same request builder and strict parser as live shadowing with an injected decision client and clock.
+
+Per case record:
+
+- requested/resolved model;
+- prompt version and case ID;
+- strict parse outcome and label;
+- duration in milliseconds from an injected monotonic clock;
+- optional provider cost; absent means unknown;
+- agreement metrics computed after resolution, outside the decision input.
+
