+5. Provider failure shadow launches only on terminal request failure; pure cancellation is distinguished; mixed cancellation races remain visible as failures.
+6. Transport rejection, timeout, saturation, malformed answers, unknown labels, and logger failure leave model/tool/retry/approval behavior byte-for-byte unchanged.
+7. Latency is measured; cost is optional/unknown when absent; requested and resolved model are both logged.
+8. Replay uses production builders/parsers, keeps labels separate, and performs no network in tests.
+
+## Concerns
+
+- Existing approval shadow logs `error` rather than `errorMessage`; use the structured logging contract for new events.
+- Existing Decisions transport returns `unknown`; changing it to a validated envelope must keep the approval consumer strict and compatible.
+- A global in-flight count is simple but tests must drain launched promises to prevent cross-test leakage.
+- Public conversation logs contain private user/tool content and should not be harvested as replay fixtures.
