+# IMPLEMENT report — Jev decision-shadow pilot
+
+Status: implementation writes complete and stable in worktree `jev-shadow-pilot` on branch `codex/jev-shadow-pilot`. No commit or merge was made.
+
+## Delivered behavior
+
+- Added a narrow `DecisionClient` over the existing OpenRouter Decisions transport. Responses validate the answer map, preserve requested/resolved model identity, parse proven provider cost fields, and represent absent cost as unknown.
+- Added two root-only, opt-in, observation-only consumers selected by `agent.decisionShadowModel`:
+  - tool-selection prediction from the final request plus the actual executable direct and `run_code` catalog;
+  - terminal provider-failure triage from bounded runtime evidence.
+- Root `AgentClient` resolves the shadow model and OpenRouter transport settings dynamically. It uses `agent.openrouter.apiKey` with `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` fallback and the optional configured base URL. Agent-override clients do not create the pilot.
+- Added `RUN_CODE_EXPOSED_TOOLS`, a read-only symbol getter over the exact bound built-ins plus the ready, collision-filtered turn-stable MCP catalog. Catalog snapshots carry executable identity, call path, source, schema, effect, approval capability, and MCP binding metadata.
+- Added versioned tool-selection and failure-triage prompts. Prediction state never includes observed tool selections, runtime failure category/retryability, cancellation classification, or observed outcome. Those values are attached later only as comparison labels.
+- Added application-run-loop observations at the prepared-request boundary, after tool settlement, and at terminal failure. Observer extraction and calls are guarded and never awaited, so throwing observers, malformed responses, transport failures, and logger failures cannot replace foreground outcomes.
+- Added a pilot-wide admission cap of four active observations and a bound of four completed tool predictions awaiting outcomes. Every Decisions request retains the existing 10-second transport deadline. Capacity, failures, latency, requested/resolved model, confidence, and provider-reported cost or explicit `unknown` are logged without raw prediction state.
+- Added synchronous evidence snapshots for both request classes. Later mutations cannot alter the asynchronous prediction request or comparison labels.
+- Added versioned replay fixtures and an evaluator that reuses live builders/parsers, keeps expected labels outside evidence, counts all fixtures in totals, and reports request/parse errors explicitly.
+- Added `source/services/decision-shadow/README.md` covering opt-in, sent/logged data, replay invocation, and limitations. Widened the existing OpenRouter Decisions row in `docs/plans/guard-ledger.md` to cover both consumers, their independent caps, the shared deadline, settlement, observability, rollback, and verification.
+
+## Implementation-owned paths
+
+- `docs/plans/guard-ledger.md`
